{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c71ba54d92744a2b","type":"text","text":"==The untouchable filth==","x":-60,"y":-50,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"9eebb3ce6bfb8959","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Cain as an orginization was formed first and foremost by humans for the sake of humanity. Yet despite their best efforts pure humans were incapable of ridding themselves of their sins. Thus the inhuman exorcists were honed and refined for that very purporse leaving humans safely behind a living bulwark of the sins that could be. However even among humanity there has always been the undesireables, the unclean, and the untouchable. Their presence was undeniable and no matter how much one would wish they too were human unlike the exorcists. Still they too had their uses.","x":-174,"y":-580,"width":478,"height":356},
		{"id":"4140127ddceee7d1","type":"text","text":"The reinforcement and ground support programs where a incredible success since its humble beginnings during The Great War.\n\nNow, officially the UN only have a human-qualified and trained military main force to respond to human conflict in a considerable scale.\n\nUnofficially, aside of The Corporation Host operatives and Worm voluntaries/Last Straw defense programs, there is one centered around those humans still with the will to do good and give their lives in the name of our cause\n\n*Blackout Division*","x":500,"y":-546,"width":600,"height":288},
		{"id":"0834d552b418acf1","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> In a modern era where the unnattural continues to change humanity always stays the same.","x":-133,"y":-900,"width":396,"height":160},
		{"id":"4ca1935abf44936f","type":"text","text":"*May their lives are long, and their effort seen for those who can live through them, one corpse at the time*","x":644,"y":-887,"width":312,"height":147},
		{"id":"1a7df9d59e36be8a","type":"text","text":"==The dregs==","x":-59,"y":-1195,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4f48ac09c21a8e4c","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Sourced from the international prison system and screened for their levels of compliance the untouchables are the dregs of common society. Accounting for murder and other high level felonies these individuals are selected to be used as a disposable defense force. Commonly stationed around Cain’s various headquarters the untouchables can also be requisitioned by exorcists for additional support in the field. However several exorcists have reported untouchables deserting or putting them in harms way. CASTLE has responded by lowering the scrip cost for deployments.","x":-192,"y":-1680,"width":515,"height":360},
		{"id":"548e66715684428c","type":"text","text":"==The Contract==","x":-59,"y":-1960,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"09deb41534759f00","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> It is no secret to the untouchables that they are more likely to die than anyone else in Cain. Despite this fact the more fresh faced of their members cling to the contract they were offered as a beacon of hope. After completing a 6 year work period every untouchable is ensured a clean record, a new idendity, and a one million dollar severance package. However CASTLE is quick to note only a single team of 3 untouchables: Fireteam ==GOLIATH== have ever completed their contract in the history of Cain. Still many untouchables will resort to any means to complete their contract.","x":-140,"y":-2580,"width":412,"height":420},
		{"id":"bce7d11d7acf8456","type":"text","text":"The Promise","x":676,"y":-1960,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"ccecba5a0ad59e88","type":"text","text":"*5 years of active service, that is all we ask of you, live long enough to complete this amount of active service and you will be rewarded with your request in full*\n\nThe contract given to those filling up the Blackout division are quite different of a standard operative, is a reward with a worth of gold but a prize that, at present time, only 4 individuals part of this program of hundreds upon hundreds reached.\n\nAnd only a single one of them accepted to cash in and leave","x":566,"y":-2544,"width":471,"height":384},
		{"id":"77ff8afb51b92669","type":"text","text":"==Deployment==","x":-59,"y":-2860,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"d909424e920ace51","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When depolyed untouchables often grease the wheels for exorcists with a gleeful amount of excessive force. Often used for hunting down or restricting witnesses, assisting in shows of authority, or assisting in the execution of a sin. However as situations escelate and more of them get wounded its not unheard of for untouchables to abandon their post. While these are humans CASTLE emphasizes that they are first and foremost criminals. From that point exorcists have full discression to abandon, execute, or utalize the untouchables as they see fit.","x":-210,"y":-3380,"width":552,"height":300},
		{"id":"2e4937cf90827b97","type":"text","text":"Usage of Blackout assault teams","x":677,"y":-2860,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"4a96c85b5b2ef1aa","type":"text","text":"In a world of monsters and those in its weird gray middle point, Blackout troops are just humans trained to deal with worms and hosts good enough to not become a problem and not further enough to put at risk the formation of more rogue agents and military armies against our cause\n\n*Worms do not fear death as they live through it in its life cycle*\n\n*Hosts are already slowly dying, doomed by circumstance or bad luck*\n\n*Human soldiers?*\n\n*They will see the reaper and stab you in the back if that means seeing another sunrise* ","x":582,"y":-3440,"width":440,"height":400},
		{"id":"d0d5bd116917cdbf","type":"text","text":"==Running your untouchables== ","x":-60,"y":60,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"8e4f674e6252c501","type":"text","text":"The Blackouts ","x":675,"y":-1195,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c8d1738576ff3ad6","type":"text","text":"A Blackout operative source could be varied: Those who still tried to Hunt and got arrested in an International prison, renegade groups or military divisions refusing to let go or \"give up\" in the fight presented with a chance\n\nMaybe they are instead witnesses of operatives in the accomplishment of their duty, \"hired\" with the promise of freedom and compensation once their sentence and duty is done\n\nOr just those suicidal enough to consider themselves the new generation of \"Modern Hunters\" and keep alive a tradition that although barbaric can still be given use in the present time","x":559,"y":-1680,"width":483,"height":360},
		{"id":"4cb229db1723fc32","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> All Untouchable squads are built around a single talisman called The Roster. The Roster accounts for how many untouchables are available, how much punishment they can absorb, and exactly what they can do for you. Seeing as Untouchables are highly disposable they are used liberally by both CAIN and their Exorcists thus every time you spend a member of your roster they die. To CAIN there is no difference between an Untouchable who is hurt and one that’s been killed. All dogs get put down in the end. A rookie squad starts at 4 and may rise to a maximum of 8. The only point a roster may consist of 10+ is under a Veteran Untouchable at Proficiency 3. When a squad gets equal or more than half of their Roster slashed roll 1D6 as the squad undergoes a Trauma Response. \n> \n> When the roster is filled completely the squad is considered Wiped and will no longer be available for the rest of the hunt. To determine the ultimate end of your untouchables make a fate roll and the result is howw many come back alive","x":-180,"y":380,"width":481,"height":579},
		{"id":"3c5dfcb2959768ba","type":"text","text":"==Trauma response==","x":-660,"y":640,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"c980e8950dfe4009","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Roll 1d6 on this table whenever the squad is slashed while at or past its breaking point.\n> \n> 1- Mutiny: The squad uses the mercenaries reactions (Cain P.147) Against the exorcists, with a talisman equal to their remaining roster. An exorcist may spend an action and roll authority to talk them down. On a success they stand down but will not act again this scene.\n> \n> 2/3- Break: The squad withdraws from the scene entirely. They return at the start of the next scene at -1 roster some never came back.\n> \n> 4/5- Dry: No responses until an exorcist spends an action to re-establish contact and resupply them, or until the next scene, whichever comes first.\n> \n> 6- Hold: The squad resists any negative effects and hold's their ground.","x":-1280,"y":424,"width":520,"height":492},
		{"id":"daf0ed69fab57167","type":"text","text":"==Presence==","x":640,"y":640,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"fddd098d3ac30aa0","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Untouchables are not like Exorcists. That much is obvious, but in many ways they differ, both in their use and deployment. Exorcist's function not only as precise and effective weapons, but also a magnifying glass to identify and solve the trauma's of a sin's manifestation. Untouchables are more akin to beating a problem with several hammers and hoping the problem goes away. Directed properly or supporting an exorcist, they are much more effective.","x":1080,"y":520,"width":460,"height":300},
		{"id":"02f3c730a1768042","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Untouchable Squads are always conspicuous, dressed in full armor and carrying weapons. They have a vehicle made to carry all of them around, allowing them to tail or follow the exorcists to any location remaining relatively unnoticed unless someone is already made aware of them.","x":1085,"y":120,"width":455,"height":233},
		{"id":"8b7f5f14455d8c6e","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When Untouchables are deployed and outwardly use force where it may been seen or recorded, Tension increases by +1. This may lead to the authorities or other threats in the hunt area becoming aware much more easily. The Discreet trait removes this effect","x":1820,"y":137,"width":480,"height":200},
		{"id":"a1eea50bd7452a38","type":"text","text":"==Field actions==","x":1935,"y":620,"width":250,"height":50},
		{"id":"96eedcf1532d954c","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> In the field Untouchable squads take no turns and have no initiative. They exist solely as a resource for the exorcists to expend and a target sins can exploit.","x":1870,"y":820,"width":381,"height":180},
		{"id":"f65f99df81c157c0","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When deployed a squads roster can be used through the following ways: Slash 1 Roster to Absorb 2 stress or deal 1d3 slashes, Complete a Response, or Complete an order. When stress is dealt to an untouchable squad, roster equal to half stress (rounded up) is slashed. A sin reaction that deals 5 stress kills three of your roster.","x":2480,"y":791,"width":478,"height":238},
		{"id":"8671b6cd0b8a8f0d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> An Untouchable squads has two main means of supporting exorcists that being their Orders and Responses.","x":3220,"y":835,"width":353,"height":151},
		{"id":"48e05c3bb5620e7b","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Responses are reactions that happen on an exorcist's action and do not consume anybody's turn. The squad may use one Response per round, not one per exorcist. Every squad starts with Support and Open Fire and a squad may know a maximum of 5 Traits and Responses combined.","x":3202,"y":440,"width":390,"height":240},
		{"id":"2b2295e26fc74a57","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Orders are a free action for exorcists, once per scene, to a squad within Long range. A Comms Unit (1 KP) extends this to anywhere in the hunt area. Orders are resolved with a fate roll determining if they succeed or lose Roster.","x":3172,"y":1120,"width":450,"height":186},
		{"id":"0ed7d4e643bbab76","type":"text","text":"==Recruitment and advancement==","x":1929,"y":1213,"width":263,"height":67},
		{"id":"3409885ba23f0777","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> For a collective 4 scrip paid individually or as a team the exorcists are assigned a Rookie Untouchable squad. Before or between missions the squad can be upgraded for an additional 2 scrip allowing the exorcist to either add +1 Roster (max 8) or +1 Trait or Response (max total 5). Additional for each hunt a squad survives without being Wiped allows them to receive either +1 Roster, or +1 Trait or Response.","x":1856,"y":1440,"width":410,"height":320},
		{"id":"60e7767e5aec2b0d","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Traits and Responses marked CAT 3+ may only be taken if the party's highest-CAT exorcist is CAT 3 or above. If that exorcist dies, the ability is no longer accessible for use.","x":1878,"y":1920,"width":366,"height":198},
		{"id":"702ac4bb7c27b5c5","type":"text","text":"==Veterans==","x":2480,"y":1569,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"2cfd7fc9c5c493db","type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When it comes to being an Untouchable, your life is rarely long. Being a pawn in the shadow war means your likely to be another name on the ever growing tombstone. Because of this, when one among them lasts longer they become notorious not just amongst the Graceless but the organization as a whole.","x":2964,"y":1493,"width":512,"height":212},
		{"id":"9d243f89cef9e246","x":3002,"y":1869,"width":437,"height":301,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> The \"Veterans\" as they are known are something of strange thing in the organization. Cain's higher ranks don't like giving them recognition. Even so, many Untouchables hoping to make it through their 6 years will inevitably see the value in using the Veterans as inspiration, training under them, learning their tactics and methods. Those helping Exorcist's directly get out faster after all, one way or another"},
		{"id":"1d2bbbcd6f573e10","x":2400,"y":1852,"width":465,"height":334,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> When a group of Untouchables under the control of a Player Exorcist squad survive 3 hunts total, they earn the ability to train under a Veteran. These are inherently similar to Virtues in nature, building a Proficiency level from 1 to 3 as your squad is shaped by using their particular methods. For each additional hunt the squad survives the squad gains proficiency this comes with learning a veterans tactics which will replace a trait or response permenantly. An Untouchable squad can only train under one Veteran at any given time."},
		{"id":"8d93e6016a14cc6f","x":3807,"y":859,"width":393,"height":127,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Traits, responses and orders options are present in page 6"},
		{"id":"bbbde25f39daed9f","x":2484,"y":2340,"width":298,"height":117,"type":"text","text":"> [!NOTE]\n> Veteran options are present in page 11 to 15"}
	],
